          ],
          "description": "Create a source-qualified preparation identity with source-named components with unknown list completeness. NBRC 1116, 1195, 1196 and 1200 and TOGO M2186, M2708 and M3181 explicitly use volume-dosed concentrated HCl reagent. This record denotes the qualitative source-described acid preparation, with variable or unspecified strength, not pure gaseous HCl or a certified commercial formulation. It preserves the source reagent boundary at UNDEFINED_MIXTURE granularity. NBRC 1200 prints 51.3 mL where NBRC 1195/1196 print 51.3 microlitres; these receiving-stock quantities remain unresolved and are not used to derive acid strength. Literal 25%, 32% and 35% are retained as source specifications, not normalized comparable fractions. The cited sources do not state a common percentage basis, carrier, grade or assay tolerance; the exact same-or-distinct preparation relation is unresolved. TOGO M2305/M2746 explicitly calls its 25% input concentrated, so that qualitative label does not exclude a numerical percentage. If comparable definitions and assay ranges were established, a real strength difference could be assessed; they are not established here. Before co-installing overlapping candidates, the coordinator must choose an explicit common bounded partial-material scope preserving every source context, or obtain comparable preparation/product evidence. No owner merge or arbitrary winner is selected.",
