          "description": "Create a source-qualified preparation identity with source-named components with unknown list completeness. JCM 431 and JCM 899 use nominal 25% HCl in trace-element preparation, respectively 12.5 mL and 5 mL per printed receiving stock. The common nominal acid-reagent boundary is represented without equating the two complete trace-element mixtures. Literal 25%, 32% and 35% are retained as source specifications, not normalized comparable fractions. The cited sources do not state a common percentage basis, carrier, grade or assay tolerance; the exact same-or-distinct preparation relation is unresolved. TOGO M2305/M2746 explicitly calls its 25% input concentrated, so that qualitative label does not exclude a numerical percentage. If comparable definitions and assay ranges were established, a real strength difference could be assessed; they are not established here. Before co-installing overlapping candidates, the coordinator must choose an explicit common bounded partial-material scope preserving every source context, or obtain comparable preparation/product evidence. No owner merge or arbitrary winner is selected.",
